## Implemented fixes

### Cleanup authority and whole-run aggregation

- Candidate validation and cleanup capabilities now use distinct private registry entries.
- Beginning disposal irreversibly revokes validation/apply authority while retaining cleanup-only authority until a complete cleanup is observed.
- Intermediate cleanup results are validated and accumulated in `_RunState.cleanup_observations`.
- Incomplete, invalid, raising, or source-modifying intermediate cleanup terminates as `sandbox_integrity_failure`; incomplete workspaces remain in `pending_retired_workspaces` for final retry.
- Final cleanup visits unique iteration, incumbent, and pending-retired workspaces and aggregates every cleanup observation from the whole run.
- Completed capabilities are removed from cleanup authority and are not disposed twice.
- The production disposer can verify an already-absent candidate after a post-removal failure while preserving capability authentication and source rechecks.

### Shell-safe schema-v3 commands

- Both active v3 prepare/canary renderers use one shared production helper.
- The interpreter is the exact absolute `sys.executable`, accepted only when it exists as a regular non-link file.
- Rendering requires a nonempty bounded argv of exact strings and an absolute executable.
- NUL, CR, LF, double quote, and all required `cmd.exe` metacharacters are rejected before `subprocess.list2cmdline`.
- Legacy command rendering was not changed.

### Canonical schema-v3 Usage recovery

- Every nested recovery `usage` value must be the exact dataclass key set and exact primitive emitted by durable `asdict(Usage)` serialization.
- Missing default-valued keys and other noncanonical shapes are rejected before ledger restoration.
- Canonical retry restoration remains idempotent.

